==Matches==
Matches took place  between 12 June and 23 June 2010.<ref name="matchschedule">{{Cite press release |title=Match Schedule 2010 FIFA World Cup South Africa |url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/64/42/24/fifawc2010matchschedulefinalversion.pdf |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091228213032/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/64/42/24/fifawc2010matchschedulefinalversion.pdf |url-status=dead |archive-date=28 December 2009 |format=PDF |date=9 December 2009 |access-date=6 December 2009|website=FIFA.com|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association}}</ref> All times listed are local, [[UTC+02:00|UTC+2]].<ref name="matchschedule"/>

===England vs United States===
The opening match of group C was contested between England and the United States.<ref name="ENGUSA">{{cite news|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_05/default.stm |title=England 1–1 USA |author=Phil McNulty |publisher=BBC Sport |date=12 June 2010 |access-date=10 November 2023}}</ref> The two sides had previously played each other nine times with England winning on seven occasions and the United States on two.<ref name="11v11USENG">{{cite news|url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/england/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/USA/ |title=England national football team: record v USA |publisher=11v11 |access-date=15 August 2023}}</ref> The teams had previously played each other once in the FIFA World Cup in [[1950 FIFA World Cup|1950]].<ref name="11v11USENG"/> The USA won [[United States 1–0 England (1950 FIFA World Cup)|1–0]] in one of the biggest World Cup shock results of all time.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44411183 |title=World Cup: England 1950 defeat by USA is 'biggest shock' |publisher=BBC Sport |date=10 June 2018 |access-date=15 August 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37363525/remembering-usa-1-0-upset-england-1950 |title=Remembering the USA's 1–0 upset of England in 1950 |author=Jeff Carlisle |publisher=ESPN |date=27 May 2014 |access-date=15 August 2023}}</ref> 

England took an early lead, [[Emile Heskey]] played a through ball to [[Steven Gerrard]] who slid the ball under [[Tim Howard]] in the 4th minute.<ref name="ENGUSA"/> However, the Three Lions failed to build on their lead, with the U.S. having plenty of possession in the first half.<ref name="ENGUSA"/> The United States equalised in the 40th minute when a seemingly harmless pot shot by [[Clint Dempsey]] was mishandled by England goalkeeper [[Robert Green]] and rolled into the net.<ref name="ENGUSA"/> Early in the second half, Heskey was played through on goal but could only shoot straight at Tim Howard.<ref name="ENGUSA"/> After several missed half-chances from England, [[Jozy Altidore]] forced a save onto the post from Green, highlighting England's lack of pace in central defence.<ref name="ENGUSA"/> Post-match, the U.S.' manager [[Bob Bradley]] was full of praise for his team's performance.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/8737319.stm |title=World Cup 2010: US coach thrilled to hold England |publisher=BBC Sport |date=13 June 2010 |access-date=10 November 2023}}</ref>

