===Algeria vs Slovenia===
The following day, Algeria met Slovenia in [[Polokwane]].<ref name="ALGSLOV">{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/sport1/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_06 |title=Algeria 0–1 Slovenia |author=Phil Dawkes |publisher=BBC Sport |date=13 June 2010 |access-date=22 November 2023}}</ref> There were few chances created throughout the first half.<ref name="ALGSLOV"/> However, in the 72nd minute, Algeria's substitute [[Abdelkader Ghezzal]] was dismissed for the accumulation of two yellow cards, the second being a handball.<ref name="ALGSLOV"/> Seven minutes later, Slovenia's talisman [[Robert Koren]] scored the winning goal from 20 yards.<ref name="ALGSLOV"/>

