===England vs Algeria===
Prior to the match, England manager [[Fabio Capello]] took the decision to drop goalkeeper Rob Green following his high-profile error against the United States, replacing him with [[David James (footballer, born 1970)|David James]].<ref name="ENGALGSKY">{{cite news|url=https://www.skysports.com/football/england-vs-algeria/211272 |title=England 0–0 Algeria: Match report & highlights |author=James Dall |publisher=Sky Sports |date=19 June 2010 |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> Algeria also opted to change their goalkeeper with [[Raïs M'Bolhi]] replacing [[Faouzi Chaouchi]].<ref name="ENGALGSKY"/> 

The match finished goalless after few chances were created by either side and with Algeria often seeming more comfortable in possession.<ref name="ENGALGSKY"/><ref name="ENGALGBBC">{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/sport1/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_23 |title=England 0–0 Algeria |author=Phil McNulty |publisher=BBC Sport |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> As England left the pitch, [[Wayne Rooney]] was heard on camera saying "Nice to see your own fans booing you." which he later apologised for.<ref name="ENGALGBBC"/><ref>{{cite news|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/8749761.stm |title=World Cup 2010: Wayne Rooney apologises to England fans |publisher=BBC Sport |date=19 June 2010 |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> Writing for ''[[Sky Sports]]'', James Dall described England's performance as unimaginative and nervy.<ref name="ENGALGSKY"/> 
